# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CBLREP admin console · environment variables
# Copy to `.env` for local work (`cp .env.example .env`).
# For Vercel: add these in Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
#
# Only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the browser bundle, and
# they are INLINED AT BUILD TIME — changing one on Vercel requires a redeploy.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1) API origin — READ THE TWO MODES BEFORE SETTING IT ON VERCEL.
#    No trailing slash, no /api suffix; the app appends /api itself
#    (src/services/adminApi.js → `${API_BASE_URL}/api`).
#
#    A · Same-origin rewrite (the deployed console's current setup):
#        leave this EMPTY. The browser calls the console's own /api/* and
#        vercel.json rewrites it to the API. No CORS preflight.
#
#    B · Direct to the API (e.g. https://api.your-domain.com):
#        set this to the API origin AND remove the /api rewrite from
#        vercel.json. Laravel CORS must allow the console origin.
#
#    Empty is also correct for `npm run dev`: the Vite proxy forwards /api/*
#    to VITE_API_TARGET below.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# 2) LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY — where the Vite dev-server proxy forwards /api/*.
#    Not used by `vite build`, so it must NOT be set in Vercel.
#    Get this machine's LAN address with:  hostname -I
VITE_API_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Backend requirements for the value above (not frontend vars):
#   • Laravel APP_URL / .env on the API host must be the public https origin.
#   • backend/config/cors.php → allowed_origins must include the Vercel
#     domain (e.g. https://cblrep-admin.vercel.app), otherwise every
#     Sanctum call fails the preflight and the console shows no data.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────